              "type": "text",
              "text": "Under a continuous exponential model, a disease doubles the number of infected individuals every week. ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If 50 people were infected at the start, after how long will 8 billion people be infected?",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Give your answer in whole weeks and the nearest day.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "27 weeks 2 days\n\nSubstitute the target population, solve with logarithms, then convert the fractional week to days.",
      "worked": "Let $w\\geq0$ be the elapsed time in weeks.\n$$\\begin{align*}50(2)^w &= 8000000000\\\\2^w &= 160000000\\\\w &= \\log_2(160000000)\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 27 whole weeks. The remaining time in days is\n$$7\\bigl(\\log_2(160000000)-27\\bigr)\\approx1.7745.$$\nTo the nearest day, the time is 27 weeks 2 days.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 20
  },
